Five Visual Wake Words classifiers, resolvable by `--model vww_<arch>`

ModelBlaster resolves --model <id> by importing modelblaster.models.<id>, so a model that
lives outside this submodule still needs a module inside it. These five are that module
and nothing else: each is ~25 lines that put $IISWC_ROOT on sys.path and defer to
fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/vision/mb_shim.py.

Exactly the split patches/0020 uses for the keyword spotters, and for the same two
reasons:

  * this submodule is a PINNED READ-ONLY input -- scripts/02_verify_patches.sh proves the
    working tree equals its base plus patches/, and an untracked model file would pass
    that gate while not surviving a fresh checkout;
  * the trained weights are ~1.3 MB of npz, which cannot be carried in a patch.

The architectures, all on MLCommons' vw_coco2014_96 corpus (109,619 COCO-2014 images,
person / no person), all fed by fpga/pynq-z2/sw/frame_fe.c from a 324x324 HM01B0 frame:

  vww_mbnet      7,157,888 MACs  the MLPerf Tiny reference shape: MobileNetV1 alpha=0.25,
                                 depthwise-separable throughout
  vww_cnn        7,154,048 MACs  the SAME budget in DENSE 3x3 convolutions (-0.054 %)
  vww_cnn_tiny   1,843,328 MACs  a quarter of it
  vww_cnn_rgb    7,485,824 MACs  vww_cnn with a three-channel first layer (demosaiced)
  vww_cnn_bayer  7,651,712 MACs  vww_cnn fed the RAW Bayer mosaic as four 48x48 planes

The first pair is a controlled architecture experiment and the last pair a controlled
sensor-colour one: matched MAC budgets, one variable each. See
fpga/pynq-z2/docs/CAMERA_TASK.md for what they measure and why.

diff --git a/models/vww_cnn.py b/models/vww_cnn.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f167e59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/models/vww_cnn.py
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+"""Visual Wake Words 'cnn' -- see fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/vision/ in the iiswc-tutorial repo.
+
+Installed by patches/0070-modelblaster-vww-models.patch.  The architecture, the trained
+weights and the calibration frames live outside this submodule on purpose: the submodule
+is a pinned read-only input and a weight blob cannot be carried in a patch.
+"""
+import os
+import pathlib
+import sys
+
+_ROOT = pathlib.Path(os.environ.get("IISWC_ROOT", "/nonexistent"))
+sys.path.insert(0, str(_ROOT / "fpga" / "pynq-z2" / "modelblaster" / "vision"))
+import mb_shim  # noqa: E402
+
+_ARCH = "cnn"
+
+
+def get_model(seed: int = 0):
+    return mb_shim.load(_ARCH)[0]
+
+
+def get_sample_input(seed: int = 1):
+    return mb_shim.calib(_ARCH, 1)[0]
+
+
+def get_calibration_samples(n: int):
+    return mb_shim.calib(_ARCH, n)
